  "title": "Erdős Problem #1014",
  "statement": {
    "representation": "markdown-latex",
    "text": "Let $R(k,l)$ be the Ramsey number, so the minimal $n$ such that every graph on at least $n$ vertices contains either a $K_k$ or an independent set on $l$ vertices.\nProve, for fixed $k\\geq 3$, that $ \\lim_{l\\to \\infty}\\frac{R(k,l+1)}{R(k,l)}=1. $ ",
